# Competency question: "Which data, model, estimator, and assumptions are on record for
# this result, and by which process?"
# Exercises the models-and-estimation spine: a math:Estimate names its math:Estimator
# (math:estimator) and its math:Estimand (math:estimatesEstimand) and is produced by a
# math:InferenceRun process (gmeow:wasGeneratedBy). The run declares each model it applied
# (gmeow:used a math:FittedModel). The data and the assumptions belong to that model, never
# to the run: the math:FittedModel carries its math:DatasetMatrix (math:fittedToData) and
# its math:ModelAssumption (math:modelAssumption). Data shared with some other model
# creates no link, so a model the generating run did not use yields no row.
#
# One row per (estimate, run, model used by the run, assumption). A run that used several
# models yields rows for all of them: the query never picks one model and never claims the
# model is unique. A row means "declared as used by the generating run", not "uniquely
# produced this estimate". An estimate whose run used no math:FittedModel yields no row.
#
# Profile: estimand-bearing estimates only (math:estimator AND math:estimatesEstimand). A
# parameter-only estimate (math:estimatedParameter plus math:estimator) is valid under the
# canonical Estimate contract and is simply outside this profile, not invalid.
# Scoped to the fixture namespace so each answer is exactly the enumerated rows.
PREFIX math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>

SELECT ?estimate ?run ?data ?model ?estimator ?estimand ?assumption WHERE {
    ?estimate a math:Estimate ;
              math:estimator ?estimator ;
              math:estimatesEstimand ?estimand ;
              gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ?run .
    ?run a math:InferenceRun ;
         gmeow:used ?model .
    ?model a math:FittedModel ;
           math:fittedToData ?data ;
           math:modelAssumption ?assumption .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?estimate), "http://example.org/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?estimate ?model ?assumption
